86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (NTPC School of Business \(NSB\) inaugurated a Capacity Building Programme on Policy and Regulatory Aspects of Electricity Distribution for officials of Distribution Companies \(DISCOMs\) under Part-B of the Revamped Distribution Sector Scheme \(RDSS\), Ministry of Power, Government of India, on 18 August 2026. The project was successfully secured through Open Competitive Bidding and is led by Dr Brijesh Bhatt. Under the project, NSB has been empanelled to conduct programmes in two key areas: Policy and Regulatory Aspects of Electricity Distribution and Financial Aspects of Electricity Distribution, aimed at strengthening the knowledge and capabilities of officials from Distribution Companies \(DISCOMs\) and State Electricity Regulatory Commissions \(SERCs\). The project envisages the conduct of 20 programmes, with an outreach target of approximately 500 officials from DISCOMs and SERCs. Through this project, NSB continues to contribute to professional development and capacity building in the power sector. The Second batch of the program is also set to commence. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
